Package: kelixip-mod-sip-servers
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Emmanuel BUU <emmanuel.buu@ives.fr>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://www.ives.fr/
Depends: kelixip (= @VERSION@)
Description: Remote SIP servers of a domain, for kelixip
 The remote SIP servers a domain exchanges calls with: application servers,
 proxies and trunks. Each server's URIs are probed by OPTIONS, and a call skips
 one known to be down; a trunk registers its account and answers the
 operator's challenges; a proxy's remote AORs are probed and reported to
 presence. Servers are declared with kelictl, the REST API or kelescope, and
 kept in the module's file. Enable it with a [module.sip_servers] block in
 config.toml.
 .
 The payload is BEAM bytecode, but the package is architecture-dependent on
 purpose: it must be built and shipped alongside the core whose embedded ERTS
 will load it.
